Task 1 — Part of #1047 (product): yoyo config get and yoyo config show still hang forever when .yoyo.toml is a FIFO (a named pipe). The assessment measured this at HEAD: both commands sat until timeout 5 killed them. The fix should be close to zero lines: swap the two plain file reads in src/commands_config.rs for the existing read_regular_to_string. That file is at 1,993 lines, so the 2,000-line cap is close; the task says to count before committing.
• `config set`: the task probes this first. Swapping the read alone isn't enough here: an empty read would lead to writing into the FIFO, which blocks too. So the fix is to refuse with an error naming the file. src/config.rs has only 11 lines of headroom, so the task counts the lines that refusal actually adds. If it's more than 8, the task leaves it out and records the measured count on #1047, rather than deferring on headroom without a number.
• Tests go in tests/config_fifo.rs, with a check that a normal .yoyo.toml still reads.
• Ticket: the task ends by posting the fixed rows and the commit sha on #1047.

